<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Virtues" cic="CCC 1803-1845" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">To use after class or in group discussion.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What is a virtue according to the Catechism? How is it acquired?</li>
<li>What are the four cardinal virtues? Why are they called &laquo;cardinal&raquo;?</li>
<li>How do the theological virtues differ from the cardinal virtues?</li>
<li>What are the three theological virtues?</li>
<li>What are the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit? What are they for?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Which cardinal virtue do you feel you need to cultivate most in your life? Why?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. How is your faith, hope, and charity reflected in your daily life?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Do you know someone who is a living example of a particular virtue? What do you admire about them?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Which gift of the Holy Spirit would you most like to ask for in prayer?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. What concrete action can you take this week to grow in a specific virtue?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. The Tree of Virtues</h4>
<p>Draw a large tree. On the roots write the cardinal virtues (prudence, justice, fortitude, temperance). On the trunk write the theological virtues (faith, hope, charity). On the branches write the gifts of the Holy Spirit. On the fruit write the fruits of the Holy Spirit. Color and decorate your tree. Place it somewhere visible this week as a reminder.</p>

<h4>B. The Week&rsquo;s Challenge</h4>
<p>Choose ONE virtue to work on this week. Each day, actively look for an opportunity to practice it. At the end of the week, write what you learned.</p>

<h4>C. Letter to a Saint</h4>
<p>Write a brief letter to a saint known for a particular virtue. Ask for their intercession to grow in that virtue. It could be St. Teresa of Avila (fortitude), St. Thomas More (justice), St. Joseph (temperance), St. Thomas Aquinas (prudence).</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;Put on then, as God&rsquo;s chosen ones, holy and beloved, compassion, kindness, humility, meekness, and patience&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">Colossians 3:12</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>
Lord Jesus,<br />
You who are the perfect model of every virtue,<br />
grant me the grace to grow in the cardinal virtues:<br />
prudence to discern the good,<br />
justice to give each his due,<br />
fortitude to persevere in the good,<br />
temperance to order my heart.<br />
Increase in me faith, hope, and charity,<br />
and pour out the gifts of Your Holy Spirit<br />
that I may bear fruits of love, joy, and peace.<br />
Amen.
</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

</LessonLayout>
